# Fase 8 · Clientes: búsqueda en caja, alta rápida, listas de precio, historial y privacidad (sin UI)
# Uso: Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code (extensión REST Client).
# Antes: dev-db.ps1 (aplica las migraciones 021–026) y `dotnet run --project src/Server/Pos.Server.Host`.
# Se supone la tienda de http/fase-07.http: cajera (código 200, PIN 5937), productos con existencias y la jornada abierta.
# Las mejoras de proveedores (bloque 8.4) están en http/fase-08-proveedores.http.

@host = http://localhost:5480
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### 1. Propietario (backoffice): lista de Empleados −5 % con redondeo a $50 y promociones; lista Mayorista fija sin promociones
# @name owner
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "dueno", "password": "Sup3rmercado-Seguro" }

@ownerToken = {{owner.response.body.token}}

###
# @name employees
POST {{api}}/catalog/price-lists
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "EMPLEADOS", "name": "Empleados", "pricesIncludeTax": true, "adjustmentPercent": -5, "roundingIncrement": 50, "allowsPromotions": true }

###
POST {{api}}/catalog/price-lists
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "MAYORISTA", "name": "Mayorista", "pricesIncludeTax": true, "allowsPromotions": false }

### 2. Grupo de clientes con su lista
# @name group
POST {{api}}/customers/groups
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "EMPLEADOS", "name": "Empleados de la tienda", "priceListId": "{{employees.response.body.id}}" }

### 3. Política de datos: la plantilla sembrada queda pendiente hasta que el propietario la revise y la active
# @name policies
GET {{api}}/customers/privacy-policies
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

###
POST {{api}}/customers/privacy-policies/{{policies.response.body.$[0].id}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 4. Cajera: buscar por cédula, celular o nombre
# @name pos
POST {{api}}/auth/pos-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "posCode": "200", "pin": "5937" }

@token = {{pos.response.body.token}}

###
GET {{api}}/customers/lookup?q=1020304050
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Alta rápida con la autorización verbal (se lee el aviso corto de la política)
# @name customer
POST {{api}}/customers/quick
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personType": "NATURAL", "identificationType": "CC", "identificationNumber": "1020304050", "firstNames": "Juan", "lastNames": "Pérez Gómez",
  "phone": "300 123 4567",
  "consents": [ { "purpose": "Service", "granted": true } ]
}

@partyId = {{customer.response.body.customer.partyId}}

### 6. Propietario: el cliente al grupo Empleados (la cajera no puede: 403)
PUT {{api}}/customers/{{partyId}}/pricing
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "groupId": "{{group.response.body.id}}" }

### 7. Venta: al asignar el cliente se re-precian las líneas con su lista; "pide factura" exige correo
# @name sale
POST {{api}}/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{api}}/sales/{{sale.response.body.id}}/lines
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "ARROZ-500", "quantity": 1 }

###
PUT {{api}}/sales/{{sale.response.body.id}}/customer
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "partyId": "{{partyId}}", "invoiceRequested": true }

### 8. Completar el correo que falta (solo campos vacíos) y cobrar
POST {{api}}/customers/{{partyId}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "juan@example.com" }

###
POST {{api}}/sales/{{sale.response.body.id}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "payments": [ { "paymentMethodId": "<id del efectivo>", "amount": 5000 } ] }

### 9. Historial y resumen (supervisor, contador o administración; requiere la autorización SERVICE del cliente)
GET {{api}}/customers/{{partyId}}/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

###
GET {{api}}/customers/{{partyId}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 10. Privacidad: tablero, solicitud del titular (vence en días hábiles), exportación y supresión
GET {{api}}/customers/privacy-status
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

###
POST {{api}}/customers/data-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "partyId": "{{partyId}}", "type": "Query", "channel": "Email", "detail": "Solicita copia de sus datos personales" }

###
POST {{api}}/customers/{{partyId}}/export
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

###
POST {{api}}/customers/{{partyId}}/anonymize
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Solicitud de supresión del titular" }
